The relationship between autonomic reactivity to emotion or affective disorders (anxiety, depression):
- Anxiety, depression (STAI-B, BDI) were measured by these questionnaires, defining as the dysregulated autonomic reactivity to emotion (自主神经系统对情绪的反应失调）
- The key symptom of anxiety and depression is the excessive avoidance
- Autonomic reactivity measurements of affective disorders: 
  SC: autonomic arousal measure of the sympathetic nervous system (sensitive index of physiological arousal) => depression patients show the lower average level of activation
  HR: physiological measure reflecting the dynamic relationship between the sympathetic and parasympatheic nervous systems (交感神经系统和副交感神经系统动态关系的生理指标）

This is the relationship between behavior (avoidance), emotion (affective disorder: anxiety and depression), autonomic reactivity (psychophysiology)



